# sha256 of lowercase tokens that must never appear in tracked text.
#
# The plaintext is deliberately absent. This repository is public, and a gate
# that listed the strings it guards would publish them on every clone and echo
# them into every public CI log on a match — which is the leak it exists to
# prevent. Only hashes live here, and the scanner reports a hash prefix, never
# the matched text.
#
# Add one:
#   printf '%s' "$token" | sha256sum | awk '{print $1}'   # or: shasum -a 256
#
# Lowercase the token first. Tokens are split on [^A-Za-z0-9._-]+, so a
# hostname and its `.local` form are two different tokens — hash both. Same for
# each numbered member of a host family.
0573015b58279e612ce5f5df0e1a8e9f12a5956beb19e4431d0d1d56829a7ccd
